# `ORDivLoc`: the bridge from node N6's division ring to the hypothesis `DivLoc`

This directory builds the vocabulary and the theorems that turn the conclusion of the JZLA20
engine (node N6, `Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.thm61Step_nonempty` + the induction
`Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isDivisionRing_of_full`) into

`Work.ORFinal.DivLoc K G φK` :

for every **locally indicable** subgroup `H ≤ G`, the division closure `D H = D_{K[H]}(U(G))` of
the field embedding `φK : K →+* ℂ` is a division ring.

## The route

Nothing in node N6 is universe-polymorphic (`Submission.Work.Section6.StepA` and
`ORHughesFree.Section6.*` are all stated at `Type`), so the bridge factors through the
**`∗`-regular closure** `V = U_N` of the image of `K[H]` in `U(G)`:

* `Work.ORDivLoc.starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H` — the `∗`-regular closure
  `R(K[H], U(G)) = starRegularClosure (starSubringClosure (Set.range (toUK E φK H))) ⊆ U(G)`;
* `Work.ORDivLoc.starClosureCod` — the induced map `K[H] →+* V`; its image generates `V` as a
  `∗`-regular ring, so it is **epic** (`Work.ORDivLoc.isEpic_starClosureCod`), which is what the
  node N6 engine needs (`thm61Step_nonempty` takes `IsEpic φ`);
* `Work.ORDivLoc.StarClosureDivOn E φK H` — "`V` is a division ring": the conclusion of the node
  N6 engine at `(K, H, V)`;
* `Work.ORDivLoc.StarClosureDivLoc K G φK` — the same for every locally indicable `H ≤ G` and the
  canonical envelope `countableEnvelope G`.

The mathematical content of the bridge (`DivisionClosure.lean`) is that `V` is *division closed*
in `U(G)` (so `D H ⊆ V`) and that `D H` is itself division closed in `U(G)`: hence a nonzero
`x ∈ D H` is a unit of `V`, its inverse lies in `V ⊆ U(G)`, and that inverse is therefore in
`D H`. This is exactly "reduce to `ℂ` and the `∗`-regular closure" of the route design (R4).

The conversion of the N5 vocabulary (`Work.ORVonNeumann.*`) into the N6 vocabulary
(`Work.ORHughesFree.*`, `Work.Section6.*`) is in `Converter.lean`, and the discharge of
`StarClosureDivLoc` from the JZLA20 engine plus Proposition 3.11 is in `N6.lean`.
-/
import Submission.Work.ORBridgeLinnell.Basic
import Submission.Work.ORBridgeLinnell.Countable
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.DivisionClosure
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.StarRegular
import Submission.Work.ORLocInd.Basic

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

universe u v

namespace Work.ORDivLoc

open Work.ORHughesFree

variable {G : Type v} [Group G] {K : Type u} [Field K]

/-! ## The `∗`-regular closure of the image of `K[H]` in `U(G)` -/

/-- **The `∗`-regular closure `V = R(K[H], U(G))`** of the image of `K[H]` in `U(G)`, inside
`U(G)`: the smallest `∗`-regular `∗`-subring of `U(G)` containing the image of `K[H]` under the
structure map `toUK E φK H`.

This is the ring to which the JZLA20 engine (node N6) is applied in the bridge: it is generated by
the image of `K[H]` (so the structure map is epic), it is `∗`-regular and positive definite
(because `U(G)` is), and it carries the faithful rank function obtained by restricting `rk_G`. -/
noncomputable def starClosureOfSubgroup (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G)
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) : StarSubring E.U :=
  starRegularClosure (starSubringClosure (Set.range (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK E φK H)))

/-- The image of `K[H]` lies in its `∗`-regular closure. -/
theorem range_toUK_subset_starClosure (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G)
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) :
    Set.range (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK E φK H) ⊆ (starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H : Set E.U) :=
  fun _ hx => subset_starRegularClosure _ (subset_starSubringClosure _ hx)

/-- **The map `K[H] →+* V`** into the `∗`-regular closure `V = R(K[H], U(G))` of the image of
`K[H]` in `U(G)`.  Its image generates `V` as a `∗`-regular ring, so it is epic
(`isEpic_starClosureCod`); this is the map to which the node N6 engine is applied. -/
noncomputable def starClosureCod (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G)
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) :
    MonoidAlgebra K ↥H →+* ↥(starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H) :=
  (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK E φK H).toRingHom.codRestrict
    (starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H).toSubring
    (fun x => range_toUK_subset_starClosure E φK H ⟨x, rfl⟩)

/-- The involution of a `∗`-subring commutes with the coercion to the ambient ring (it is the
definition of the involution on the subtype). -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_star_starSubring {U : Type*} [Ring U] [StarRing U] (S : StarSubring U) (x : ↥S) :
    ((star x : ↥S) : U) = star (x : U) := rfl

@[simp]
theorem starClosureCod_apply (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G)
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) (x : MonoidAlgebra K ↥H) :
    ((starClosureCod E φK H x : ↥(starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H)) : E.U) =
      Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK E φK H x := rfl

/-! ## The two properties the bridge relates -/

/-- **Node N6's output at the `∗`-regular closure `V`**, in the exact form in which the induction
of [JZLA20, Theorem 6.1] delivers it
(`Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isUnit_of_mem_divisionClosure`, which needs no epicity hypothesis):
every nonzero element of the division closure `D_{K[H],V}` of the image of `K[H]` in `V` is a unit.

By `isUnit_of_mem_divisionClosure`, this follows from the existence of the induction environments
`Work.ORHughesFree.Thm61Step K ↥H V φ H₀` for every finitely generated non-trivial `H₀ ≤ ↥H`
(the construction `thm61Step_nonempty`); that construction is the open gap of node N6 and is the
hypothesis of `Work.ORDivLoc.clDivOn_of_hstep`. -/
def ClDivOn (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ)
    [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) : Prop :=
  IsDivisionRing ↥(divisionClosure (Set.range (starClosureCod E φK H)))

/-- **Node N6's conclusion at `(K, H, V)`**, in the form delivered by
`Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isDivisionRing_of_full`: the `∗`-regular closure `V` of the image of
`K[H]` in `U(G)` is a division ring.  This route additionally needs `IsEpic φ` (which holds
because `V` is generated by the image of `K[H]`), and is used in
`Work.ORDivLoc.starClosureDivOn_of_clDivOn`. -/
def StarClosureDivOn (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ)
    [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) : Prop :=
  IsDivisionRing ↥(starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H)

/-- **The conclusion of the bridge**, in the form of the body of `Work.ORFinal.DivLoc`: every
nonzero element of the division closure `D E φK H = D_{K[H]}(U(G))` is a unit. -/
def DivOn (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U]
    (H : Subgroup G) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : ↥(Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D E φK H), x ≠ 0 → IsUnit x

/-- **The hypothesis of the bridge, for every locally indicable subgroup and the canonical
envelope**: for every locally indicable `H ≤ G`, the `∗`-regular closure of the image of `K[H]`
in `U(G) = countableEnvelope G` is a division ring.

This is the form in which the JZLA20 engine (node N6, `thm61Step_nonempty`) plus
[JZLA20, Proposition 3.11] deliver the analytic input (see `N6.lean`). -/
def StarClosureDivLoc (K : Type u) [Field K] (G : Type v) [Group G] [Countable G]
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK
  ∀ H : Subgroup G, Work.ORLocInd.Group.LocallyIndicable H →
    StarClosureDivOn (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK H

/-- **Node N6's output, as a hypothesis over a whole group.**  For every locally indicable
`H ≤ G`, the division closure `D_{K[H],V}` of the image of `K[H]` in the `∗`-regular closure `V`
of that image is a division ring.  This is the exact conclusion of the induction of
[JZLA20, Theorem 6.1] at the `∗`-regular closure, and is the hypothesis under which
`Work.ORDivLoc.divLoc_of_clDivLoc` discharges `DivLoc`. -/
def ClDivLoc (K : Type u) [Field K] (G : Type v) [Group G] [Countable G]
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK
  ∀ H : Subgroup G, Work.ORLocInd.Group.LocallyIndicable H →
    ClDivOn (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK H

/-- **`DivLoc` itself**, in the form in which `Work.ORFinal` uses it, restated here so that the
bridge does not depend on the (separately maintained) `Work.ORFinal` module.  It is
*definitionally* `Work.ORFinal.DivLoc K G φK`; see `Work.ORDivLoc.divLoc_eq_orFinalDivLoc`. -/
def DivLoc (K : Type u) [Field K] (G : Type v) [Group G] [Countable G]
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK
  ∀ H : Subgroup G, Work.ORLocInd.Group.LocallyIndicable H →
    DivOn (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK H

end Work.ORDivLoc
